  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Donken – the M with a diagonal pass and finish at speed",
  "description": "One line in each corner at one end and a cone on each side further out towards the middle. A runs without the ball down along the boards, rounds the cone and turns in towards the slot. B plays a diagonal pass from the other corner and A shoots first time. Then B runs the same way on their side and gets the pass from the next player in line A. The running paths make an M.\n\nRotation: after the shot, join the other line, so everyone shoots from both sides. A quick warm-up for both players and goalkeeper. Variants: let the next player in your own line pass from behind (one line is enough, run it from both corners), or put the lines out by the sides level with the centre line – the runner goes diagonally towards the cone on the other side near the goal, receives, rounds the cone and shoots. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Full speed through the whole run, round the cone too."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Show with your stick where you want the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The pass should be flat and in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Shoot first time – do not stop to receive."
    }
  ],
